From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:04:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Initialize the batch flush admission before it is read

PipelineBroadcastExchange::FlushReadyBatches() declares its
AppendAdmission without a value and assigns it only when a batch is
ready. It reads it only on that path too, because the loop returns
first when no batch is ready, but GCC 13 does not connect the two and
-Wmaybe-uninitialized reports the read. The admission starts out as
BLOCKED, which the assignment replaces before any read.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/src/parallel/pipeline_broadcast_exchange.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/parallel/pipeline_broadcast_exchange.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/parallel/pipeline_broadcast_exchange.cpp
index 84db381bd9..f0dba515a1 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/parallel/pipeline_broadcast_exchange.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/parallel/pipeline_broadcast_exchange.cpp
@@ -1156,7 +1156,7 @@ PipelineBroadcastExchange::FlushReadyBatches(idx_t min_batch_index, const Interr
 		vector<ExchangeLogEntry> log_entries;
 		vector<InterruptState> readers;
 		vector<InterruptState> writers;
-		AppendAdmission admission;
+		AppendAdmission admission = AppendAdmission::BLOCKED;
 		AppendReservation reservation;
 		shared_ptr<DataChunk> copy;
 		bool has_ready_batch;
